   "ref": "60–64",
   "en": "Dido herself, loveliest of all, holds the offering-dish in her right hand and pours it [between|9,10] the horns of a gleaming white cow; or walks before the faces of the gods to the altars heaped with offerings, renewing the day's gifts, and, gazing into the opened breasts of the victims, searches their still-breathing entrails for a sign.",
